---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Stream the property events of a run as they happen, until the run is final.

Each event prints as one line:

  property <property id> <name>
      A property appears for the first time.

  sample <property id> example <input hash> <vtime>
  sample <property id> counterexample <input hash> <vtime>
      An example or a counterexample of the property, the first time it
      arrives. A non-event property's sample is its value, as JSON.

  verdict <property id> passed|failed
      The property passed or failed. A verdict that repeats the last verdict
      does not print.

  completed <run id>
      The run is final, and the stream ends.

  unknown <type> <json>
      A notification that snouty cannot read, printed as its JSON.

The samples are a selection: the server does not send every example and
counterexample that it counts. To see a property and its totals, use
`snouty runs property <run_id> <property_id>`. To read the logs at a moment, use
`snouty runs logs <run_id> <input hash> <vtime>`.

The stream shows only the events that happen after it starts. It does not show
the current results. A property that passed or failed before the stream started
gets no verdict line. To get the current results and follow them, start the
stream first. When stderr says `the stream of run <run_id> is open` (or, on a
terminal, the spinner says `streaming run`), read
`snouty runs properties <run_id>` and merge the two. This order makes sure that
you do not miss an event.

The stream is silent between events. For a run that is already final, the stream
prints `completed` and ends. The stream of a new run opens a few minutes after
the run starts, and snouty waits until it opens.

If the stream ends before the run is final, snouty exits with an error. Start
the stream again, then read the current results.

Streaming needs a run created on release 65.3 or later.

Examples:
  snouty runs stream <run_id>
  snouty runs stream <run_id> --property <property_id>

Add --json for machine-readable output. Each event prints as one JSON object,
with an `event` key and the fields above. Each vtime is a JSON number. The
`data` key holds the JSON of an unknown notification:
  snouty --json runs stream <run_id> | jq -r 'select(.event == "verdict" and
  .verdict == "failed") | .property_id'

Usage: snouty runs stream [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID>

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>
          Run ID

Options:
      --property <PROPERTY_ID>
          Stream only the events of this property (repeatable)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --utc
          Show times in UTC instead of the local timezone

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
